      "id": "berklee-music-theory-book-1-p0043",
      "source_en": "Lesson 17. Half Steps and Whole Steps\n\n27 The whole step is the distance of two half steps. On the keyboard, two keys a whole step apart have one key between them.\n\n27 On the keyboard, keys next to each other, with no other key in between, whether white or black, are a half step apart, as you saw in lesson 14.",
